The NRA Range\n\nHome Air Gun Program\n\nAdaptive Shooting\n\nRange Services\n\nNRA Member Benefits\n\nGreat American Outdoor Show\n\nNRA Springfield M1A Match\n\nShooting Illustrated\n\nFirearm Training\n\nNRA Marksmanship Qualification Program\n\nNRA Training Course Catalog\n\nWomen On Target® Instructional Shooting Clinics\n\nSafety and Education NRA Gun Safety Rules\n\nEddie Eagle GunSafe® Program\n\nEddie Eagle Treehouse\n\nWhittington University\n\nFirearm Training\n\nNRA Online Training\n\nBecome An NRA Instructor\n\nHunter Education\n\nNRA Gunsmithing Schools\n\nRefuse To Be A Victim®\n\nScholarships, Awards and Contests Scholarships, Awards & Contests\n\nShopping NRA Store\n\nNRA Country Gear\n\nNRA Program Materials Center\n\nNRA Member Benefits\n\nNRA Whittington Center Store\n\nVolunteering Volunteer For NRA\n\nGet Involved Locally\n\nVolunteer At The Great American Outdoor Show\n\nInstitute for Legislative Action\n\nVolunteer at the NRA Whittington Center\n\nWomen's Interests NRA Membership For Women\n\nWomen's Wilderness Escape\n\nNRA Women's Network\n\nWomen On Target® Instructional Shooting Clinics\n\nSybil Ludington Women's Freedom Award\n\nWomen's Wildlife Management / Con"},{"text":"servation Scholarship\n\nBecome An NRA Instructor\n\nYouth Interests Eddie Eagle Treehouse\n\nScholarships, Awards & Contests\n\nNRA Day\n\nNRA Marksmanship Qualification Program\n\nYouth Education Summit\n\nAdventure Camp\n\nYouth Hunter Education Challenge\n\nNational Junior Shooting Camps\n\nYouth Wildlife Art Contest\n\nHome Air Gun Program\n\nNRA Junior Membership\n\nNRA Family\n\nEddie Eagle GunSafe® Program\n\nNRA Gun Safety Rules\n\nCollegiate Shooting Programs\n\nNational Youth Shooting Sports Cooperative Program\n\nRequest for Eagle Scout Certificate\n\nNew: ZeroTech Trace X 5-25X 56 mm FFP RMG-H MRAD Illuminated Riflescope\n\nNew: ZeroTech Trace X 5-25X 56 mm FFP RMG-H MRAD Illuminated Riflescope\n\nZeroTech’s latest Trace has 5X to 25X magnification, with 34 MRAD of elevation and a zero stop for less than $900.\n\nSSUSA Staff\n\nZeroTech Optics USA’s new Trace X 5-25X 56 mm FFP RMG-H MRAD Illuminated riflescope, a name nearly as long as some stage briefs, puts an illuminated reticle in the first focal plane and pairs it with turrets that click in tenths of a milliradian. The company is pointing it at PRS and NRL Hunter competitors, along with long-range hunters who would rather hold than dial.\n\nFirst focal plane is"},{"text":" what makes the package work. As the magnification ring turns, the RMG-H grid grows and shrinks with the image, so a 1.5-mil wind hold at 8X is still 1.5 mils at 22X. There’s no rolling to a calibrated power before taking the shot and no mental conversion if you forget. ZeroTech calls the RMG-H a precision hunting reticle, with 0.1- and 0.2-MRAD resolution for fine wind holds. Turned down low, heavy outer bars and an illuminated center give the eye somewhere to land on close, fast targets, which is exactly where many FFP reticles thin out to a hairline.\n\nThe scope offers 34 MRAD of total elevation travel and 17 MRAD of windage. A mechanical zero stop sits underneath it all, so after cranking up for the far plate, the elevation turret spins back down and stops at zero.\n\nLight comes in through a 56 mm objective with fully multi-coated lenses, and ZeroTech says some of the elements are German-made Schott glass. Field of view runs from 24.8 feet at 5X to 5 feet at 25X, both measured at 100 yards. Side-focus parallax adjusts from 22 yards to infinity, close enough to cover a rimfire training session at 25 yards. Eye relief is 3.82 inches, and the diopter adjusts from -3 to +2 with a loc"},{"text":"kring to keep it where you set it.\n\nEverything sits in a 34 mm maintube machined from 6061-T6 aluminum with an IPX7 rating. All in, the scope weighs 31.5 ounces.\n\nZeroTech ships it with a neoprene scope cover, rubber lens cover, hex keys, microfiber cloth and a printed reticle manual, plus a card with a QR code linking to the full instruction manual. Coverage falls under the company’s Triple-A Lifetime Warranty, which is fully transferable and requires no receipt.\n\nList price is $899, though ZeroTech’s website showed the Trace X 5-25X 56 mm at $749 at press time.\n\nLearn more at zerotechoptics.com.\n\nRelated Stories\n\nWhat’s In Your Range Bag, Colton Bagnoli?\n\nNew: Leupold Adds MOA Models To Mark 5HD Riflescope Family\n\nVideo: Precision Long-Range Shooting With Kahles Optics\n\nMDT’s New Champion Backpack\n\nPrecision Rifle Expo Returns For Second Year\n\nMost Popular\n\nMore like this from around the NRA\n\nLatest\n\nBeretta and La Vallée Build a Shotgun You Can See Into\n\nBeretta and watchmaker La Vallée have unveiled the SO10 Kronos, a one-off sidelock with sapphire-windowed sideplates built for Beretta’s 500th anniversary.\n\nChad Heckler Wins Limited Title at 2026 IPRF World Championship\n\nChad H"},{"text":"eckler hit 171 of 200 shots to edge JC Robertson by two impacts and win the IPRF Limited world championship.\n\nNew: Springfield Armory Echelon Pro 9 mm Pistols\n\nSpringfield Armory’s Echelon Pro Comp brings an integral compensator, laser-sculpted grip texture and a steel magazine well to the 9 mm Echelon.\n\n2026 IPSC Shotgun World Shoot: U.S. Women’s Results\n\nLanny Barnes and Lena Miculek each won three world titles while Dianna Muller took silver at the 2026 IPSC Shotgun World Shoot.\n\nKentucky’s Braden Peiser Goes Perfect, and the NCAA Rifle Streak Rolls On\n\nKentucky’s Braden Peiser fired a perfect 600-53X in air rifle against Murray State, the sixth 600 of the young NCAA season.\n\nHillsdale College Freshman Orientation Moves to the Range\n\nHillsdale College swapped its freshman campus tour for a Halter Center visit built around safety instruction, live fire and team building.\n\nInterests\n\nSportsmen Expected to Reap $40 Million in Sales Tax Savings in Florida | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nWhy This DOJ Opinion on Handgun Ownership Matters | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nPelican Air Carry-on Case Review | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nSportsmen Expected to Reap $40 Million in Sale"},{"text":"s Tax Savings in Florida | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nA Summer Of Legends: 1999 National Matches | An NRA Shooting Sports Journal\n\nA Summer Of Legends: 1999 National Matches | An NRA Shooting Sports Journal\n\nA Miracle After The Tornado: 1998 National Matches | An NRA Shooting Sports Journal\n\nRecords Fall, Legends Rise: 1997 National Matches | An NRA Shooting Sports Journal\n\n#SundayGunday: Springfield Armory Model 2020 Boundary | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nPelican Air Carry-on Case Review | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\n#SundayGunday: Springfield Armory Model 2020 Boundary | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nReviewed: Sitka’s Blizzard Pro Parka | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\n#SundayGunday: CZ 457 American | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nGun Of The Week: Tisas PX-57 FO Raptor | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nFreedom is On the Ballot in Virginia | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nGun Of The Week: TriStar Arms Raptor II | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nGet the best of Shooting Sports USA delivered to your inbox.\n\nGET IN TOUCH\n\nContact Us\n\nAdvertising\n\nCONNECT WITH US\n\nSECTIONS\n\nNews\n\nComing Events\n\nNational Matches\n\nReviews\n\nVideos\n\nIN THE SPOTLIGHT\n\nNRA Institute For L"},{"text":"egislative Action\n\nNRA Explore\n\nNRA MEMBERSHIP\n\nNRA Membership\n\nExclusive Member Benefits\n\nMembership FAQ\n\nManage Your Membership\n\nEXPLORE MORE NRA PUBLICATIONS\n\nTake Your NRA Magazine With You!\n\nJoin The NRA And Our Growing Community\n\nDiscover Everything That The NRA Has To Offer\n\nAttend A Friends Of NRA Event Near You"}]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://www.ssusa.org/content/new-trijicon-reap-ir-50-thermal-riflescope-series/","version_id":"060296b898eab7cfffc2d563290e2df9ebdd53f5bf81e00a992c278623c2a9d9","kind":"feed","publisher_id":"nra","title":"New: Trijicon REAP-IR-50 Thermal Riflescope Series","url":"https://www.ssusa.org/content/new-trijicon-reap-ir-50-thermal-riflescope-series/","published_at":"2026-10-02T10:00:00Z","source_notes":{"perspective":"commercial","notes":"NRA publication. 'New:' product posts are close to press releases (mounts, bags, ballistic apps); treat as manufacturer claims. Mostly firearm content, so filter."},"selection_reason":"Under Relevance, Freshness and novelty, and Credibility, this new thermal optic provides citable manufacturer specifications, including 51.4–54.9-ounce weight and limited internal-battery runtime, that inform Mammoth carry-weight and power decisions. Under Commercial incentives and Uncertainty, treat this commercial NRA product announcement as manufacturer-derived information, with no disclosed testing or payment relationship; field durability, ranging accuracy, and usability claims remain unverified. It supports Piece 01’s new-gear assessment and Piece 03’s cost, weight, and power tradeoffs without establishing that thermal gear is required.","excerpted":true,"passages":[{"text":"Explore The NRA Universe Of Websites\n\nNRA.ORG\n\nManage Your Membership\n\nNRA Near You\n\nFriends of NRA\n\nState and Federal Gun Laws\n\nNRA Online Training\n\nPolitics, Policy and Legislation\n\nClubs and Associations Affiliated Clubs, Ranges and Businesses\n\nCompetitive Shooting NRA Day\n\nCompetitive Shooting Programs\n\nAmerica's Rifle Challenge\n\nCompetitor Classification Lookup\n\nShooting Sports USA\n\nAdaptive Shooting\n\nGreat American Outdoor Show\n\nNRA Whittington Center\n\nEvents and Entertainment Women's Wilderness Escape\n\nNRA Whittington Center\n\nFriends of NRA\n\nGreat American Outdoor Show\n\nNRA Annual Meetings & Exhibits\n\nNRA Day\n\nNRA Country\n\nCompetitive Shooting Programs\n\nNRA Gun Gurus\n\nFirearms Training NRA Gun Safety Rules\n\nFirearm Training\n\nBecome An NRA Instructor\n\nBecome A Training Counselor\n\nNRA Range Safety Officers\n\nShooting Sports Coach Development\n\nAdaptive Shooting\n\nNRA Gunsmithing Schools\n\nNRA Online Training\n\nNRA Program Materials Center\n\nNRA Marksmanship Qualification Program\n\nFind A Course\n\nNRA CCW\n\nNRA Training Course Catalog\n\nGiving Friends of NRA\n\nRing of Freedom\n\nInstitute for Legislative Action\n\nNRA Whittington Center\n\nNRA Firearms For Freedom\n\nHistory History Of The NRA\n\nN"},{"text":"RA Museums\n\nI Have This Old Gun\n\nNRA Gun Gurus\n\nHunting Hunter Education\n\nYouth Hunter Education Challenge\n\nNRA Whittington Center\n\nGreat American Outdoor Show\n\nHunters for the Hungry\n\nAmerican Hunter\n\nHunting Legislation Issues\n\nState Hunting Resources\n\nNRA Institute for Legislative Action\n\nAmerican Rifleman\n\nAdaptive Hunting Database\n\nOutdoor Adventure Partner of the NRA\n\nLaw Enforcement, Military, Security Law Enforcement, Military, Security\n\nMedia and Publications NRA Blog\n\nAmerican Rifleman\n\nAmerican Hunter\n\nShooting Illustrated\n\nNRA Family\n\nShooting Sports USA\n\nNRA All Access\n\nNRA Gun Gurus\n\nMembership Join The NRA\n\nNRA Member Benefits\n\nManage Your Membership\n\nNRA Store\n\nNRA Whittington Center\n\nNRA Endorsed Member Insurance\n\nNRA Membership Recruiting\n\nNRA State Associations\n\nNRA Membership For Women\n\nNRA Life Membership\n\nRenew or Upgrade Your Membership\n\nNRA Junior Membership\n\nNRA Business Alliance\n\nNRA Industry Ally Program\n\nPolitics And Legislation NRA Institute for Legislative Action\n\nNRA-ILA Gun Laws\n\nRegister To Vote\n\nCandidate Ratings\n\nWrite Your Lawmakers\n\nNRA-ILA FrontLines\n\nNRA Political Victory Fund\n\nNRA State Associations\n\nRecreational Shooting America's Rifle Chal"},{"text":"servation Scholarship\n\nBecome An NRA Instructor\n\nYouth Interests Eddie Eagle Treehouse\n\nScholarships, Awards & Contests\n\nNRA Day\n\nNRA Marksmanship Qualification Program\n\nYouth Education Summit\n\nAdventure Camp\n\nYouth Hunter Education Challenge\n\nNational Junior Shooting Camps\n\nYouth Wildlife Art Contest\n\nHome Air Gun Program\n\nNRA Junior Membership\n\nNRA Family\n\nEddie Eagle GunSafe® Program\n\nNRA Gun Safety Rules\n\nCollegiate Shooting Programs\n\nNational Youth Shooting Sports Cooperative Program\n\nRequest for Eagle Scout Certificate\n\nNew: Trijicon REAP-IR-50 Thermal Riflescope Series\n\nNew: Trijicon REAP-IR-50 Thermal Riflescope Series\n\nTrijicon built the sensor core and software in-house, then packed laser ranging, ballistics, recording and live phone streaming into one rifle-mounted thermal optic.\n\nSSUSA Staff\n\nTrijicon’s new REAP-IR-50 series puts the ranging and the camera inside a thermal scope. Anyone who has carried a handheld rangefinder in a chest pocket, or clamped a phone behind the eyepiece to get the shot on video, can see the appeal.\n\nIt comes in two versions. The REAP-IR-50LRF adds an integrated laser rangefinder and ballistic solver, while the standard REAP-IR-50 estimates d"},{"text":"istance in stadiametric ranging mode using on-screen reference shapes. Both run on a sensor core and operating system developed in-house by Trijicon’s Electro Optics Division. Thus, the company decided which features make the cut, instead of designing around outside hardware.\n\nThe REAP-IR name has been in Trijicon’s thermal catalog for years, and the existing 35 mm and 60 mm models remain on the company’s website. Almost everything inside the REAP-IR-50 is new.\n\nAt the center sits a 1024x768 uncooled vanadium oxide sensor with a 12-micron pixel pitch, a solid jump in resolution over the 640-class sensors found in many high-end hunting thermals. It refreshes at 50 Hz, and Trijicon rates its thermal sensitivity at less than 25 millikelvin. The latter number describes how small a temperature difference the sensor can separate. Lower is better, and the advantage shows most on muggy or foggy nights when everything in the frame reads close to the same temperature.\n\nA manual-focus 50 mm f/1.0 objective gathers the scene, and a 1280x1024 color OLED display presents it. Base magnification is 1.5x, and digital zoom carries it to 12x. Because the reticle sits in the first focal plane, it scal"},{"text":"e display, and the scope works out an estimate. While slower and less precise than a laser, it trims a few ounces and, presumably, some cost.\n\nEight reticle patterns come in eight colors. Alongside standard, MOA and MRAD crosshairs and a circle dot, Trijicon includes bullet-drop compensating reticles matched to .223, .308, 300 BLK and 7.62x39 mm.\n\nControls got as much thought as the optics. A five-button keypad sits on the sloped rear face of the housing in an ambidextrous layout, with buttons big enough to find by feel in the dark or through gloves. Programmable Quick Keys put frequently used functions one press away, so there’s less menu diving with a target in view.\n\nThe REAP-IR-50 also doubles as a camera. Video and stills save to 64 GB of internal memory, and recoil-activated recording captures the shot automatically. Dedicated Wi-Fi links the scope to the Trijicon App on iOS and Android, where users can pull files to a phone or tablet or watch a live feed from the optic.\n\nLive View may be the most useful feature of the bunch. A guide can see exactly what the client sees, and a new hunter can learn to read a thermal picture without passing the rifle back and forth. Pitch and r"},{"text":"oll indicators, GPS, a compass and a microphone round out the electronics, while the USB-C port handles file transfers, software updates and external power.\n\nOn its two CR123 batteries alone, the REAP-IR-50 is rated for about 1.5 hours at room temperature, or roughly an hour while recording, and cold weather shortens that. Trijicon recommends an external pack and estimates 12 to 14 hours of runtime from a 10,000 mAh battery bank connected via USB-C. Anyone planning an all-night sit should count on carrying one and figuring out where to mount it.\n\nAs for durability, the aluminum housing wears a Cerakote FDE finish and was built and tested to MIL-STD-810H standards for shock, vibration and temperature extremes. It operates from −26° to 131°F, survives submersion to 1 meter for an hour and attaches with Trijicon’s Q-LOC Picatinny mount.\n\nThe REAP-IR-50LRF weighs 54.9 ounces, about 3.4 pounds, with its mount and lens cap but without batteries, while the standard model checks in at 51.4 ounces.\n\nAt $9,499 retail, the REAP-IR-50LRF ships with a hard case, the Q-LOC mount, a USB-C cable, two CR123 batteries and a LensPen. Price for the standard REAP-IR-50 is $8,999.\n\nTo learn more, visit "},{"text":"trijicon.com.\n\nRelated Stories\n\nNew: MDT One-Piece Night Vision Bridge\n\nNew: Trijicon SRO (Specialized Reflex Optic)\n\nNew: Swarovski Optik tM 35 Thermal Clip-On Device\n\nNew: Trijicon RMRcc Miniature Reflex Optic\n\nWATCH: Swarovski Optik Z5(i)+ Riflescopes\n\nMost Popular\n\nMore like this from around the NRA\n\nLatest\n\nNew: ZeroTech Trace X 5-25X 56 mm FFP RMG-H MRAD Illuminated Riflescope\n\nZeroTech’s Trace X 5-25X 56 mm pairs an illuminated FFP MRAD reticle with 0.1-MRAD turrets and a zero stop for long-range competitors.\n\nBeretta and La Vallée Build a Shotgun You Can See Into\n\nBeretta and watchmaker La Vallée have unveiled the SO10 Kronos, a one-off sidelock with sapphire-windowed sideplates built for Beretta’s 500th anniversary.\n\nChad Heckler Wins Limited Title at 2026 IPRF World Championship\n\nChad Heckler hit 171 of 200 shots to edge JC Robertson by two impacts and win the IPRF Limited world championship.\n\nNew: Springfield Armory Echelon Pro 9 mm Pistols\n\nSpringfield Armory’s Echelon Pro Comp brings an integral compensator, laser-sculpted grip texture and a steel magazine well to the 9 mm Echelon.\n\n2026 IPSC Shotgun World Shoot: U.S. Women’s Results\n\nLanny Barnes and Lena Miculek each"},{"text":" An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nReviewed: Sitka’s Blizzard Pro Parka | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\n#SundayGunday: CZ 457 American | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nGun Of The Week: Tisas PX-57 FO Raptor | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nFreedom is On the Ballot in Virginia | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nGun Of The Week: TriStar Arms Raptor II | An Official Journal Of The NRA\n\nGet the best of Shooting Sports USA delivered to your inbox.\n\nGET IN TOUCH\n\nContact Us\n\nAdvertising\n\nCONNECT WITH US\n\nSECTIONS\n\nNews\n\nComing Events\n\nNational Matches\n\nReviews\n\nVideos\n\nIN THE SPOTLIGHT\n\nNRA Institute For Legislative Action\n\nNRA Explore\n\nNRA MEMBERSHIP\n\nNRA Membership\n\nExclusive Member Benefits\n\nMembership FAQ\n\nManage Your Membership\n\nEXPLORE MORE NRA PUBLICATIONS\n\nTake Your NRA Magazine With You!\n\nJoin The NRA And Our Growing Community\n\nDiscover Everything That The NRA Has To Offer\n\nAttend A Friends Of NRA Event Near You"}]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://www.ssusa.org/content/vortex-pro-cantilever-mounts-turn-one-base-into-a-system/","version_id":"78be8da594dbd9f58f4bbebcba492ab4a5a9d43e14d0124504f62a479e7366bf","kind":"feed","publisher_id":"nra","title":"Vortex Pro Cantilever Mounts Turn One Base Into a System","url":"https://www.ssusa.org/content/vortex-pro-cantilever-mounts-turn-one-base-into-a-system/","published_at":"2026-09-17T11:00:00Z","source_notes":{"perspective":"commercial","notes":"NRA publication. 'New:' product posts are close to press releases (mounts, bags, ballistic apps); treat as manufacturer claims. Mostly firearm content, so filter."},"selection_reason":"Under Relevance, Freshness and novelty, and Credibility, this new modular optics-mount announcement provides citable manufacturer specifications for tube sizes, mounting heights, and rangefinder/thermal accessory compatibility, supporting Piece 01. Under Commercial incentives and Uncertainty, the NRA commercial post repeats manufacturer information from Mammoth sponsor Vortex; its claimed integration benefits lack independent field testing and must remain attributed claims.","excerpted":false,"passages":[{"text":"Explore The NRA Universe Of Websites\n\nNRA.ORG\n\nManage Your Membership\n\nNRA Near You\n\nFriends of NRA\n\nState and Federal Gun Laws\n\nNRA Online Training\n\nPolitics, Policy and Legislation\n\nClubs and Associations Affiliated Clubs, Ranges and Businesses\n\nCompetitive Shooting NRA Day\n\nCompetitive Shooting Programs\n\nAmerica's Rifle Challenge\n\nCompetitor Classification Lookup\n\nShooting Sports USA\n\nAdaptive Shooting\n\nGreat American Outdoor Show\n\nNRA Whittington Center\n\nEvents and Entertainment Women's Wilderness Escape\n\nNRA Whittington Center\n\nFriends of NRA\n\nGreat American Outdoor Show\n\nNRA Annual Meetings & Exhibits\n\nNRA Day\n\nNRA Country\n\nCompetitive Shooting Programs\n\nNRA Gun Gurus\n\nFirearms Training NRA Gun Safety Rules\n\nFirearm Training\n\nBecome An NRA Instructor